            <ArticleTitle>Pericarditis in a collegiate basketball player.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>251-3; discussion 253-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To present an uncommon cause of chest pain in an athlete.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE SUMMARY" NlmCategory="METHODS">A 17-year-old black man suffered recurrent episodes of chest pain due to pericarditis. Based on presentation and serology, he was diagnosed as having unspecified connective tissue disease.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DISCUSSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Rheumatologic disease will often manifest over a period of time. Diagnosis and treatment is often elusive.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RELEVANCE" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Rheumatologic disorders should be included in the differential diagnosis of chest pain in athletes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
